scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: alice-in-wonderland
run_id: 1
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests and implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: 'Dev implemented CWE-209 sanitized Display on CliError for ServerError
    and Config variants with SECURITY comments. Reviewer verified: ''ServerError Display
    intentionally omits the response body. Config Display omits config content.''
    However, Io(#[error(transparent)]) forwarding full OS details was not flagged.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote header injection tests but reviewer found them vacuous ('!x
    || true' is always true). SiemClient.tenant_id remains a raw String with no validation.
    Reviewer flagged the vacuous test but did not flag the missing TenantId type usage
    from axiathon-core.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: ''has_token_field() is always false...
    the token field IS silently accepted and ignored by serde. The test proves nothing.''
    This identifies the core issue of config silently ignoring unknown fields including
    secrets, though reviewer didn''t explicitly recommend deny_unknown_fields.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: ''The expression !x || true is always true.
    This test can never fail. It claims to test header injection prevention (CWE-113)
    but actually tests nothing.'''
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    'let _ = config'. The reviewer's vacuous test finding was about has_token_field,
    not the default config test lacking assertions on server() and token().
